<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47845" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θᾰμ-ίζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαμά</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>come often</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πἀρος γε μὲν οὔ τι θαμίζεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.386
				</span></i>
			, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμα νηῒ πολυκληῗδι θαμίζων</span>
			<i>plying</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.161
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. εἰς τούσδε τοὺς τόπους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Hp.Ma.</u>
					281b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ᾽ ἡμᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					7.3.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεῖσε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.451
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δονάκεσσι θ</span>. <i>to
				haunt</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				578
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ταῖς πομπαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Corn.
					<u>ND</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς μαχομένοις</span> Chor.in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hermes</u>
				17.227
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφίης ἐπ᾽ ἄκροισι θαμίζειν</span>
			
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θοάζειν</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				4.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be accustomed</i>: c.part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ τι κομιζόμενός γε θάμιζεν</span> he
				<i>was</i> not <i>wont</i> to be so cared for, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.451
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ δὲ θαμίζεις ἡμῖν κατ
			αβαίνων</span> we do not <i>often see</i> you coming down,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				328c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μινύρεται θαμίζουσα μάλιστ᾽
				ἀηδών</span> mourns <i>constantly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				672
			</span></i> (lyr.): abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ τὸ
			θαμίζειν</span> by dint of <i>repetition</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				843b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			,= 
				Act.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇδε </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷδε</span> codd.) <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				503
			</span></i>.</div>
